kind how-do-i
title How do I set an effect, such as an amber tint, on a look?
intro An effect is a vtlook: a file of filters that vtium applies to everything a terminal draws, such as a color tint. A look's card names its vtlook, and the Effects tab lists the vtlooks this machine has.
see looks/make-a-look-and-use-it-on-the-console

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [look plain]
    palette = legacy
    [head console]
    vt = 5
    look = plain
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
file etc/looks/amber.vtlook
    version = 1
    [color tint]
    color = 255,176,0
    amount = 1.0
    floor = 0.0

1. Go to the Looks tab.
2. Choose plain.
3. Set vtlook to amber.
4. Press Esc.
5. Press s to save.
6. Press i to install.
7. Press y.
at the install
check draft look plain vtlook amber
check installed head console look plain
check installed look plain vtlook amber
